## 3. Evidence plan

Every work unit carries exactly one evidence obligation. `DETERMINISTIC` evidence is discharged
by re-running a command and comparing; `CITATION` evidence is discharged by resolving references
and confirming each carries its sub-claim.

| ID | WU | Claim | Kind | Reproducible check | A miss means |
|----|----|-------|------|--------------------|--------------|
| EV-0 | WU-0 | Protocol frozen before any data contact | DETERMINISTIC | `wc -lc plan/preregistration/S-PROBE-protocol.frozen.md` → `162 8052`; frontmatter `frozen_at` precedes `SelectionRecord.frozen_at` | thresholds may have been fitted to the data; run is void |
| EV-1 | WU-1 | The probed spec text is pinned and §4.3 is enumerable | DETERMINISTIC + CITATION | `sha256(spec/SAEOS-1.md)` equals report `spec_sha`; every `FieldMatrix` row resolves to its cited §4.3 line range | the denominator is unpinned — the loss ratio measures nothing specific |
| EV-2 | WU-2 | The 3 goals are sealed, and were chosen by a stated rule before extraction | DETERMINISTIC + CITATION | `<sealed_filter> \| wc -l` equals `candidate_count`; each `seal_ref` resolves; `frozen_at` precedes all verdicts | the sample may be the convenient goals, not real sealed ones |
| EV-3 | WU-3 | Each corpus is closed and re-derivable | DETERMINISTIC | re-run the traversal from the ledger entry; sorted file list is byte-identical; `closure_size` equals its `wc -l` | extraction had a side door; `ABSENT` counts are not trustworthy |
| EV-4 | WU-4 | Every cell is scored, and every claim resolves inside its closure | DETERMINISTIC | row count equals `3 × Σ(fields per node type)`; every citation path is a member of that goal's closure list | skipped cells silently remove losses from the denominator — bias toward GO |
| EV-5 | WU-5 | The adversary pass ran and had teeth | CITATION | every non-`ABSENT` cell has `challenged: true` + outcome; downgrade count stated; zero-downgrade pass carries a justification | the challenge is decorative; vacuous citations survive (`CANARY-0002`) |
| EV-6 | WU-6 | Every number is recomputable from the report's own tables | DETERMINISTIC | recount labels from the three per-goal tables, reapply the frozen weights, reproduce all six ratios; check `lenient ≤ headline ≤ strict` | the verdict rests on arithmetic nobody can check |
| EV-7 | WU-7 | The verdict follows from the ScoreSheet and the frozen thresholds | DETERMINISTIC | re-evaluate D1–D5 against `## score sheet` using the frozen file; same verdict, same `failed_predicates`; frozen-file pin re-verified | thresholds may have moved mid-run |
| EV-8 | WU-8 | The report matches the §10 contract | DETERMINISTIC | `rg -n '^## ' <report>` yields the nine section headers in order; `rg -c '^## goal: '` is exactly 3 | the acceptance gate passes or fails for format reasons unrelated to the finding |
