## 10. Handoff

The EXECUTE stage needs: write on `reviews/spikes/`; read on `spec/`, `ledger/`, `reviews/tasks/`
and `plan/preregistration/`. It should run WU-1…WU-9 in the order of §4, discharge one evidence
item per unit as that unit closes, and abort to `BLOCKED` with the matching escalation — not
improvise — if `ASM-1`, `ASM-2`, `ASM-3`, `ASM-4` or `ASM-5` fails.

The single instruction that matters most: **a NO-GO is a successful outcome** (`…:387`). The
spike costs three hand-extractions and either saves the build or clears it. Nothing in this plan
should be read as pressure toward GO — the tie-break, the downgrade-only challenge, the
capability-enforced freeze and the `R-VOID` class all exist to lean the other way.
